{"content":"P2: Move focus into the dialog after it becomes visible. Opening the dialog from a focused button leaves focus on that button, although the calendar selector is enabled. Select an enabled dialog control, or the dialog itself when no control is available.","codeSuggestion":"","assessment":"Confirmed accessibility defect. The edit location is in unchanged code.","rationale":"PositionedDialog.show() sets visibility to hidden before it calls the native show method. It restores visibility after positioning but does not set focus. CalendarEventCreateEditDialog.show() returns that result without setting focus. Keyboard input therefore remains outside the newly opened dialog.","recommendation":"change","validation":"The headless Thunderbird check recorded open: true, visibility: visible, selectorDisabled: false, and focusInside: false. document.activeElement remained the opening button. The existing keyboard test calls before.focus() at browser_calendarEventCalendarSelector.js:407, so it does not check initial focus. Minimum test coverage: focus an opening control, open the dialog, and assert focus inside the dialog without a later focus() call.","appliedSummary":"Updated [calendar-event-create-edit-dialog.mjs](/Users/aschmitz/.tb-tools/worktrees/task-ebd62b49-ca85-47a3-85a2-02eccd78dc96/comm/mail/components/calendar/content/calendar-event-create-edit-dialog.mjs:402) to focus the enabled selector, or the dialog when selection is unavailable.

Added tests in [browser_calendarEventCalendarSelector.js](/Users/aschmitz/.tb-tools/worktrees/task-ebd62b49-ca85-47a3-85a2-02eccd78dc96/comm/mail/components/calendar/test/browser/browser_calendarEventCalendarSelector.js:166). They cover initial focus and focus preservation on repeated show calls.

Verification passed: headless browser test with accessibility checks, lint, syntax checks, and `git diff --check`.","changeSummary":"Set initial focus after the create/edit dialog becomes visible.","state":"handled","changeAccepted":false,"changeReverted":false,"changesAmended":true}
